# ApexTick - rules for AI assistants working in this repo
(Read HANDOFF.md first: it has the architecture, accounting rules, history and open work.)

## What this is
Python/Flask crypto trading bot for Binance: spot "accumulator" + USDT-M futures "sniper", SMC (order-block / FVG) zone entries,
BTC macro gate, macro-news kill switch, SQLite ledger, web dashboard. It runs in PAPER mode. LIVE trading is deliberately locked.

## Hard rules
1. Never enable or "fix toward" LIVE trading unless the user explicitly says so. Keep ALLOW_LIVE_TRADING gating, fail-safe mode flags
   (LIVE only when paper_trading_enabled == "0"), and the ADMIN_KEY checks. LIVE order code is known-unsafe (see HANDOFF.md section 16).
2. Safety principles: fail CLOSED on missing/stale data (BTC gate, prices), fail SAFE on settings (anything but an explicit value = PAPER).
3. Never commit or print secrets or data: .env, apextick.db(-wal/-shm), API keys. Keep the repo private.
4. SQL is always parameterised with "?" via database.execute_query / execute_batch. Balance changes are RELATIVE updates
   ("x = x + ?"), never "x = <value read earlier>" (the dashboard and engines write concurrently).
5. Do not change trading behaviour as a side effect of a UI/analysis task. Config changes go through config.py dicts.

## Working agreement with the user
- If the user says "brainstorm" / "discuss" / "explain": talk only, do NOT write or edit code. Ask before building.
- Explain in plain language, give exact copy-paste commands (the user sometimes types Python at the bash prompt by mistake).
- Deliver complete files plus tests. State plainly what changed and what did NOT change.
- Be honest about uncertainty. Paper results are optimistic (no real fills); one market episode is not proof.

## How to run / verify
- Tests (each suite uses its own temp SQLite DB, no network): `python3 run_all_tests.py`   -> expect "ALL GOOD" (9 suites, 201 checks)
- Dashboard UI test (jsdom): `cd tools && npm install && node ui_test.js`   -> expect "FAILED: none" (55 checks)
- App: `python3 app.py` (needs .env; dashboard on :5000). DB: ./apextick.db (SQLite, WAL).
- Test fixtures: set SQLITE_DB_PATH to a temp file BEFORE importing database; mark prices fresh with
  MARKET_STATE["prices_ts"] = time.time() + 10**9; set futures_engine.PAPER_SLIPPAGE_PCT = 0.0 when asserting exact numbers.

## Conventions
- Engines run every 3s in threads started by app.py. Shared price/BTC state lives in btc_decline_signal.MARKET_STATE.
- templates/dashboard.html uses CRLF line endings and is a Jinja template ({{ bot_name }}); escape all server data with esc() before innerHTML.
- Add a test for every behaviour change; keep the existing suites green.
